 Texas A&M Corps of Cadets","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The Corps site lists Monday–Friday, 8 a.m.–5 p.m.; confirm access before a weekend visit.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tamu-bonfire-memorial","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Bonfire Memorial","title":"Visit the Bonfire Memorial thoughtfully","subtitle":"Memorial site on campus","notes":"Walk the Spirit Ring slowly, read the portals and reflections, and keep the visit quiet and respectful of the people memorialized there.","short_summary":"A campus memorial interpreting the 1999 Bonfire collapse.","evidence_claim":"Texas A&M states that Bonfire Memorial was dedicated at the site of the 1999 Bonfire collapse and includes the Spirit Ring and 12 portals.","source_url":"https://www.tamu.edu/campus-community/traditions/remembrance/bonfire-memorial.html","source_title":"Bonfire Memorial | Texas A&M University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"On-site tours are offered by MSC Hospitality; request one in advance if desired.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tamu-memorial-student-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Memorial Student Center","title":"Make the MSC your reset stop","subtitle":"275 Joe Routt Boulevard","notes":"Use the MSC as a central indoor break: locate services, check event postings, and plan the next stop before heading back outside.","short_summary":"A central campus facility with services, vendors, and event spaces.","evidence_claim":"The Memorial Student Center hosts vendors, services, dining and entertainment, and lists its physical address at 275 Joe Routt Boulevard.","source_url":"https://ucenter.tamu.edu/facilities/memorial-student-center/","source_title":"Memorial Student Center | Texas A&M University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The page lists summer hours of 7 a.m.–8 p.m. Monday–Saturday and 10 a.m.–8 p.m. Sunday; verify seasonal hours.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tamu-aggie-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Aggie Park","title":"Take an outdoor pause at Aggie Park","subtitle":"Between Alumni Center and Koldus Building","notes":"Choose a bench or open lawn for a low-key break, then look for the water features and performance pavilion before continuing your walk.","short_summary":"A 20-acre campus park with water features and gathering space.","evidence_claim":"Texas A&M describes Aggie Park as a 20-acre outdoor space with an amphitheater, water features, an ice cream shop, and a performance pavilion.","source_url":"https://www.tamu.edu/campus-community/life-in-aggieland/campus-destinations.html","source_title":"Campus Destinations | Texas A&M University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use public park areas and follow any event signage or temporary access restrictions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tamu-gardens","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"The Gardens at Texas A&M University","title":"End with a daylight garden walk","subtitle":"556 John Kimbrough Boulevard","notes":"Finish in daylight with a self-guided walk through the public gardens; take photos from paths and leave when it gets dark as requested.","short_summary":"A free public garden for a calm final stop.","evidence_claim":"The Gardens at Texas A&M are free to visit, open daily from dawn to dusk, and open to campus visitors and the public.","source_url":"https://gardens.tamu.edu/visit/admission-hours